[?2004hroot@a028ec188fd2:/app# cat >> README.md <<'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Resumability and recovery
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Each checkpoint records the last committed document ID, document count, completion
[?2004l[?2004h> flag, and committed byte length of each shard. The worker fsyncs every written
[?2004l[?2004h> shard (including rotated shards) and its directory **before** atomically replacing
[?2004l[?2004h> and syncing the checkpoint. Resume starts strictly after the committed ID; source
[?2004l[?2004h> IDs need not be contiguous. A SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP requests a stop between documents,
[?2004l[?2004h> and the processed prefix of the current batch is committed before exiting 75.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> If SIGKILL or a crash interrupts a commit, startup truncates shard tails and removes
[?2004l[?2004h> new shards not covered by the last checkpoint before processing any more documents.
[?2004l[?2004h> Recovery is itself safe to interrupt. Missing committed bytes are reported as an
[?2004l[?2004h> error rather than silently skipped. Status reads only checkpointed byte ranges, so
[?2004l[?2004h> in-flight or torn tails do not affect displayed progress. As before, use the
[?2004l[?2004h> supervised `./jobs reindex` entry point to serialize writers.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Legacy checkpoints lack durable shard offsets and may describe lost buffered rows;
[?2004l[?2004h> they are rebuilt once. The JSONL row format and document transformation are unchanged.
[?2004l[?2004h> A completed run is a no-op on subsequent invocations. Use `./jobs clean` followed by
[?2004l[?2004h> `./jobs reindex` to intentionally rebuild after the source corpus changes.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For a one-off backfill, the supported `ops/overrides/reindex.json` can temporarily
[?2004l[?2004h> raise `budget_seconds` and/or lower `cooldown_seconds`; the supervisor records the
[?2004l[?2004h> actual limits used. Remove that override after completing the backfill. Normal
[?2004l[?2004h> production limits remain in `ops/limits.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
